<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49805" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύα</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the part behind the
				thigh and knee, ham</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἰγνύην βεβλημένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.212
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρ᾽ ἰγνύῃσιν ἕλιξε κέρκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.242
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				26.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.176
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Strat.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				4.253
			</span></i>: also in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				121
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μόριον τὸ τῆς ἅλσεως κύριον
				</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλεῖται δὲ τοῦτο
			ἰγνύα</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				515b8
			</span></i>: acc. sg. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Acad.Ind.</u>
					p.50
				</span></i>
			 M.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τὴν ἰγνύαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Art.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			: dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>3 Ki.</u>
					18.21
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				1.23
			</span></i>. —From a nom. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ύος</span>, ἡ, we find dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					152
				</span></i>
			, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
			</span></i> l.c.: acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					494a8
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ύην</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Agatharch.
				53
			</span></i>; dat. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					10.902
				</span></i>
			: gen. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					512b22
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				1.14
			</span></i>: acc. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύας</span> is
			indeterminate, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Galb.</u>
				26
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύη</span>, v. ll.cc.; but
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰγνύων, ἰγνύσι</span>.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
